        *   If a cell value contains a comma (`,`) or a double quote (`"`), it's enclosed in double quotes.
        *   Any existing double quotes within the cell are doubled (`"` becomes `""`) to comply with CSV standards.
    *   It prints the cell values to the CSV file, separated by commas.
    *   A separator (`\n---\n\n`) is added between sheets to distinctly show where one sheet ends and another begins in the CSV.
    *   It closes the Excel file and the CSV file.
